  "stem": "The incomplete table shows the sophomores and juniors at a high school and whether they are in the robotics club. If a sophomore is selected at random, the probability that the student is in the robotics club is \\(\\frac{1}{6}\\). If a member of the robotics club is selected at random, what is the probability that the student is a junior?",
  "figure": {
    "kind": "table",
    "title": "Robotics club membership",
    "columns": [
      "Grade",
      "In robotics club",
      "Not in robotics club",
      "Total"
    ],
    "rows": [
      [
        "Sophomore",
        "",
        "",
        "180"
      ],
      [
        "Junior",
        "",
        "",
        "150"
      ],
      [
        "Total",
        "48",
        "",
        "330"
      ]
    ]
  },
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "3/8"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Sophomores in the club: \\(\\frac{1}{6}(180) = 30\\).",
    "Juniors in the club: \\(48 - 30 = 18\\).",
    "The probability is \\(\\frac{18}{48} = \\frac{3}{8}\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "r = figure['rows']\nsoph = Rational(1, 6) * int(r[0][3])\njun = int(r[2][1]) - soph\nassert soph == 30 and jun == 18\nassert [Rational(a) for a in spr_answers] == [jun / int(r[2][1])]",
